123:In this study, we aimed to understand the biological heterogeneity of autism by identifying potential neuroanatomical subtypes within a large and well-phenotyped cohort. To do so, we employed spectral clustering on the individual-level deviations from a normative model of CT development. Normative modeling learns supervised mappings that describe cortical development, also accounting for sex and nuisance variation. This allows the clustering algorithm to focus upon clinically relevant variation better than by clustering the data directly and
